<!--
  Notification icon.

  Android renders a notification icon as a silhouette: every non-transparent
  pixel is recoloured white, and the alpha channel is all that survives. So
  the glyph cannot be drawn on top of the bubble in another colour — it has to
  be an actual hole. One path, evenOdd fill: the outer bubble winds one way,
  the chevron and caret inside it wind the other, and the overlap becomes
  transparent.

  A terminal prompt inside a speech bubble: a session asking you something,
  which is the only reason this app ever notifies.
-->
